    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0006438 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0006438">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001641"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005218"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Cells of this line contain HeLa marker chromosomes, and were derived via HeLa contamination. This line was originally thought to be derived from an epidermoid carcinoma of the larynx, but was subsequently found, based on isoenzyme analysis, HeLa marker chromosomes, and DNA fingerprinting, to have been established via HeLa cell contamination. The cells are positive for keratin by immunoperoxidase staining. ATCC confirmed this cell line is positive for the presence of human papilloma viral DNA sequences via PCR.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.utsouthwestern.edu/about-us/administrative-offices/technology-development/industry/human-cancer-cell-lines.html</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HEp-2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


