    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007042">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001444"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>quantification in a sample of some polychlorinated biphenyls, a group of man-made environmental pollutants which accumulate in humans with adverse health effects</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <efo:gwas_trait rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</efo:gwas_trait>
        <rdfs:label>polychlorinated biphenyls measurement</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007047 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007047">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Toxoplasma gondii seropositivity is the result of a measurement of circulating T. gondii specific antibodies. T. gondii is a parasitic protozoan that causes toxoplasmosis</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <efo:gwas_trait rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</efo:gwas_trait>
        <rdfs:label>Toxoplasma gondii seropositivity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007048 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007048">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>human herpesvirus 6 seropositivity is the result of a measurement of circulating human herpesvirus 6 specific antibodies</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <efo:gwas_trait rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</efo:gwas_trait>
        <rdfs:label>human herpesvirus 6 seropositivity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007049 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007049">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>gliadim seropositivity is the result of a measurement of circulating  antibodies specific to the food antigen gliadin</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>gliadin seropositivity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007050 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007050">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HSV1 seropositivity is the result of a measurement of circulating herpes simplex virus type 1 specific antibodies </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <efo:gwas_trait rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</efo:gwas_trait>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>herpes simplex type 1 seropositivity</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>HSV1 seropositivity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007054 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007054">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001444"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>quantification of microsatellite instability</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Dani Welter</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <efo:gwas_trait rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</efo:gwas_trait>
        <rdfs:label>microsatellite instability measurement</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007057 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007057">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001444"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A measure of how fast cancer cells are dividing and growing. To find the mitotic rate, the number of cells dividing in a certain amount of cancer tissue is counted. Mitotic rate is used to help find the stage of melanoma (a type of skin cancer) and other types of cancer. Higher mitotic rates are linked with lower survival rates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Catherine Leroy</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MR</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Definition taken from : http://www.cancer.gov/publications/dictionaries/cancer-terms?cdrid=681122</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>miotic rate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007058 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007058">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0004949"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The date or time of the last check of a patient by a medical professional.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Catherine Leroy</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>last follow up</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007061 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007061">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001444"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The number of times a cell culture has been passaged (sub-cultured or split). </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Catherine Leroy</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>passage number</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007069 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007069">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000010"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mouse 3134 is a murine mammary adenocarcinoma cell line generated in Dr. Gordon Hager’s laboratory at the National Institutes of Health, Bethesda, MD.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>https://genome.ucsc.edu/ENCODE/protocols/cell/mouse/3134_Stam_protocol.pdf</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>3134</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007070 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007070">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001639"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0001641"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>ACC112 was established from a salivary glad tumor of a 70-year-old male. Adenoid cystic carcinoma cell line supplied by Lurdes Queimado, M.D., Ph.D. Phone: 405-271-4232 (office); 405-271-4279 (lab); cells immortalized by infection with a retrovirus expressing HPV16 E6 and E7</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10328235</efo:definition_citation>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>UTSW-ACC112</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>ACC112</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007071 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007071">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The hES line BG01 with a normal 46XY karyotype was derived from fibroblasts of an embryonic male human.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.iscr-admin.com/Default.aspx?Action=viewsc&amp;StemCellLine=62&amp;StemCelName=BG01</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>BG01</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007072 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007072">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005292"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A B-lymphoblastoid cell line derived from a randomly selected Caucasian blood donor whose parents and grandparents were born in the UK or Ireland. The cell line was generated by Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV) transformation of peripheral blood lymphocytes. This cell line is part of the European Collection of Cell Cultures (ECACC) Human Random Control (HRC) collection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.sigmaaldrich.com/catalog/product/sigma/94060845?lang=en&amp;region=US</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>C0202</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007073 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007073">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This hESC line was isolated using human feeder cells under good manufacturing process (GMP) conditions. NIH registration: 0041.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://discovery.lifemapsc.com/stem-cell-differentiation/in-vitro-cells/inner-cell-mass-homo-sapiens-cyt49-viacyte-novocell-san-diego-ca</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>CyT49</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007074 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007074">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002937"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>DND-41 was established from the peripheral blood of 13-year-old boy with T-acute lymphoblastic leukemia (T-ALL; type III cortical) in 1977; described to carry CDKN2B (p15INK4B) and CDKN2A (p16INK4A) deletions and TP53 (p53)mutation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>https://www.dsmz.de/catalogues/details/culture/ACC-525.html</efo:definition_citation>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CLO:0009834</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>RRID:CVCL_2022</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ACC525</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>DND-41</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007075 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007075">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002887"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mouse embryonic stem cell line E14.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM1014154</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>ES-E14</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007076 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007076">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The I3 stem cell line was derived from donated blastocysts by removal of the trophoblast layer and further culturing of the intact inner cell mass on mitotically inactivated mouse embryonic fibroblast (MEF) feeder cells. Following injection into SCID mice, the I3 line formed teratomas that contained tissues from all three embryonic germ layers. This line exhibits a normal XX karyotype. These cells were provided by Alex Meissner and maintained in mTeSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM537624</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>ES-I3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007077 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007077">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005292"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lymphoblastoid cells taken from the blood of a female human.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM659931</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>GM06999</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007078 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007078">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XY karyotype, pluripotency tested in vitro and in vivo. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including SSEA-3, SSEA-4, TRA-1-60, TRA-1-81, and alkaline phosphatase. [DOI: 10.1056/NEJMsr040330]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on 10% KOSR (Invitrogen) medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsr040330</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES13</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007079 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007079">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XX karyotype, pluripotency tested in vivo (teratoma). The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including OCT4, SSEA-4, TRA-1-60, TRA-1-81, and alkaline phosphatase. [PMCID: PMC3335201]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3335201/</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES28</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


