    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007088 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XY karyotype. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including OCT4, and NANOG. [PMCID:PMC3335201]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3335201/</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES63</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007089 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007089">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XY karyotype. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including OCT4, and NANOG. [PMCID:PMC3335201]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3335201/</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES64</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007090 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007090">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005730"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>HUES64 cells were differentiated into CD184+ endothelial cells in feeder free conditions, using RPMI containing 100ng/mL of Activin A and 50ng/mL of Wnt3a, for 5 days. On day 5, the CD184 positive population was sorted via FACS. Cells come from a healthy male embryo provided by Harvard University.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM772725</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES64-derived CD184+</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007091 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007091">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XY karyotype. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including OCT4, and NANOG. [PMCID:PMC3335201]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3335201/</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES65</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007092 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007092">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including OCT4, NANOG, and TRA-1-60. [PMCID:PMC3335201]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3335201/</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES66</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007093 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007093">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with a normal 46XY karyotype, pluripotency tested in vitro and in vivo. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including SSEA-3, SSEA-4, TRA-1-60, TRA-1-81, and alkaline phosphatase. [DOI: 10.1056/NEJMsr040330]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsr040330</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES8</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007094 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007094">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005738"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human embryonic stem cell line with an abnormal 46XX, Inv9 karyotype, pluripotency tested in vitro and in vivo. The stem cells were derived from human blastocysts and are strongly positive for a number of molecular markers of undifferentiated pluripotent human stem cells, including SSEA-3, SSEA-4, TRA-1-60, TRA-1-81, and alkaline phosphatase. [DOI: 10.1056/NEJMsr040330]. Cells were provided by Harvard University and maintained on KSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsr040330</efo:definition_citation>
        <rdfs:label>HUES9</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007095 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007095">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005740"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>IPS DF 19.7 cell line is an induced pluripotent stem cell line, derived from newborn foreskin fibroblasts. Cells were received from the James Thomson laboratory, who originally reprogrammed the cells from fibroblasts provided by ATCC (Cat# CRL-2097TM). The first set of numbers before the period refer to different clones, the number after the period indicates the sub-clone. The differentiation method is described here: http://www.sciencemag.org/cgi/content/full/324/5928/797?rss=1</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM665800</efo:definition_citation>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19325077</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>iPS DF 19.7</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007096 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007096">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002888"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005740"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Human induced pluripotent stem cell line line derived from foreskin fibroblasts, isolated as described by Yu, J. et al. Human induced pluripotent stem cell lines free of vector and transgene sequences. Science 324, 797-801 (2009). Cells were received from the James Thomson laboratory, who originally reprogrammed the cells from fibroblasts provided by ATCC. The first set of numbers before the period refer to different clones, the number after the period indicates the sub-clone. Cells were maintained on mTeSR medium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM752965</efo:definition_citation>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19325077</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>iPS DF 19.11</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


