        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0005740"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>IPS DF 4.7 cell line is an induced pluripotent stem cell line, derived from newborn foreskin fibroblasts. Cells were received from the James Thomson laboratory, who originally reprogrammed the cells from fibroblasts provided by ATCC (Cat# CRL-2097TM). The first set of numbers before the period refer to different clones, the number after the period indicates the sub-clone. The differentiation method is described here: http://www.sciencemag.org/cgi/content/full/324/5928/797?rss=1</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <efo:definition_citation>http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSM665803</efo:definition_citation>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19325077</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>iPS DF 4.7</rdfs:label>
