        <obo:IAO_0000115>In psychology, the quantification of the interval of time between the presentation of a stimulus to a subject and the beginning of the subject&apos;s response to that stimulus. Several categories of reaction time, such as simple reaction time and choice reaction time, have been established and studied in experimental psychology to assess general alertness and motor speed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
